                20,
                24
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "PrCgT1",
                  "fill": "#EF4444",
                  "content": "⚠️  The CGNAT Problem (most people hit this)",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "bold"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "PrCgT2",
                  "fill": "#EF9999",
                  "content": "Most ISPs now use CGNAT (Carrier-Grade NAT) — you share a public IP with neighbors.\nThis means:\n• Port forwarding doesn't work at all\n• Telegram/WhatsApp webhooks can't reach your Mac\n• SSL certificates via HTTP-01 challenge fail\n• Your OpenClaw agent is invisible to the internet\n\nWorkaround: rent a VPS as a tunnel ($5/mo) + set up WireGuard + Cloudflare.\nAt that point, you're paying $5/mo for the tunnel + $14/mo for the Mac Mini = $19/mo.\nAgentPuter: $9/mo with everything included. No tunnel. No workaround.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "PrCmpNote",
              "width": 780,
              "fill": "#1A1A1A",
              "cornerRadius": 8,
              "stroke": {
                "thickness": 1,
                "fill": "#FFAA3340"
              },
              "gap": 6,
              "padding": [
                12,
                20
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Pr5_217",
                  "fill": "#FFAA33",
                  "content": "🤝  Honest note",
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Pr5_218",
                  "fill": "#FFAA33",
                  "content": "If you already own a Mac Mini, have a static IP (no CGNAT), disabled auto-sleep,\nand don't mind SSH-ing in to fix things — self-hosting OpenClaw is totally fine.\nAgentPuter is for people who just want to talk to their agent without becoming a sysadmin.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "Inter",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
